                      <property name="validator_style">wxFILTER_NONE</property>
                      <property name="validator_type">wxDefaultValidator</property>
                      <property name="validator_variable"></property>
                      <property name="value">-setup VNAX pair using mmwave macro&#x0A;-connect in thru with a big attenuator in between&#x0A;    -it should be more than the gain of your amp&#x0A;-run the power calibration (2nd tab)&#x0A;-after the cal. algorithm runs the pna should switch to a linear sweep with very low power (-30 to -29dbm input)&#x0A;   -verify this is the case before you proceed&#x0A;-add your amplifier (DUT)&#x0A;-note: input of DUT has to be on P1, output of DUT on attenuator&#x0A;-the attenuator should be between DUT and P2&#x0A;-run the compression test (3rd tab)&#x0A;    -the &quot;check setup&quot; button will show what power ranges you are about to sweep&#x0A;    -you can run multiple amps using the same power calibration&#x0A;    -but for safety the power cal won&apos;t save when the program closes&#x0A;-plot whatever you want on the (4th tab)&#x0A;-data exports in longform .csv, ask JJG for tips on plotting in excel&#x0A;-this program can alternatively be used just to generate plots from previous data&#x0A;-SND&amp;TJR 05/2025</property>
                      <property name="window_extra_style"></property>
                      <property name="window_name"></property>
                      <property name="window_style"></property>
                    </object>
